# ============================================================================
# Real access control for /portfolio/  (Apache / cPanel / most shared hosting)
# ============================================================================
#
# The JavaScript gate on these pages is obfuscation. It stops a casual
# visitor; it does not stop anyone who opens View Source, and it does not
# protect portfolio/docs/*.pdf from being fetched directly.
#
# This file does. It makes the web server itself demand credentials before it
# sends a single byte of anything in this directory, including the PDF.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TO ACTIVATE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  1. Rename this file to exactly ".htaccess" (drop the .example).
#
#  2. Create the password file OUTSIDE your web root, so it can never be
#     downloaded. On cPanel this is usually /home/<user>/:
#
#         htpasswd -c /home/<user>/.rivosus-htpasswd investor
#
#     It will prompt for a password twice. To add more people later, run the
#     same command WITHOUT -c (the -c flag creates a new file and wipes any
#     existing one):
#
#         htpasswd /home/<user>/.rivosus-htpasswd secondperson
#
#  3. Correct the AuthUserFile path below to match step 2.
#
#  4. Load https://www.rivosus.com/portfolio/ and confirm the browser asks for
#     a username and password. Then confirm the PDF is protected too, by
#     opening it directly in a private window:
#
#         /portfolio/docs/BlueJay%20-%20Rivosus%20-%20Potential%20Uses.pdf
#
#     If that prompts for credentials, you are covered. If it downloads, stop
#     and recheck the path in step 3.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

AuthType Basic
AuthName "Rivosus Ranch - Private Circulation"

# EDIT THIS PATH. It must point outside the web root.
AuthUserFile /home/CHANGEME/.rivosus-htpasswd

Require valid-user

# Belt and braces: tell crawlers to stay out at the header level as well as
# in the page <head>, in case a file here is ever served without its markup.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet"
  Header set Referrer-Policy "no-referrer"
</IfModule>

# Never allow directory listings here.
Options -Indexes
